IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-interpretation`
IMPORT `g6-art20-court-orders`

-- g6-tests-art20.l4: tests of Article 20 (Court orders as to fitness of governor).
-- Every expected value was decided from the text of the Law before the module was first run; the quotation above a group is the text it comes from.
-- A DEONTIC cannot be compared in #ASSERT, so powers and prohibitions are exercised by #TRACE, each with its outcome in the `-- EXPECT:` comment above it
-- (read by work/g6/check-traces.py); the facts behind them are asserted on the BOOLEAN and DATE rules.

§ `Tests of Article 20`

§§ `Article 20(1) -- the orders the court may make`

-- src:514 | (1) On an application under Article 19(9)(b) or (13), the court may make any order that the court sees fit, including without limitation –
-- src:515 | (a) an order dismissing the application;
-- src:516 | (b) an order giving permission for the governor to act as a governor despite a reportable matter;
-- src:517 | (c) an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity;
-- src:518 | (d) an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor;
-- src:519 | (e) an order making any provision that could be made by a required steps notice;
-- src:520 | (f) any order ancillary to any such order.
-- (1) On an application under Article 19(9)(b) or (13), the court may make any order that the court sees fit, including (a) to (f). One test per kind: made on an application, it discharges the permission.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1) the court may make the order` TRUE `any other order that the court sees fit` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `any other order that the court sees fit` AT 12
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(a) the court may make an order dismissing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order dismissing the application` AT 12
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(b) the court may make an order giving permission for the governor to act as a governor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order giving permission for the governor to act as a governor despite a reportable matter` AT 12
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(c) the court may make an order that the entity must not be registered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity` AT 12
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(d) the court may make an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor` AT 12
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(e) the court may make an order making any provision that a required steps notice could make` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order making any provision that could be made by a required steps notice` AT 12
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(f) the court may make an order ancillary to any such order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order ancillary to any such order` AT 12
-- An order of another kind is not the one the limb permits: the permission of limb (c) is not used by an order of kind (a).
-- EXPECT: STANDING make an order on the application
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(c) the court may make an order that the entity must not be registered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make an order on the application` `the court` `an order dismissing the application` AT 12
-- A permission not used stands; and without an application there is nothing the court may do under the paragraph.
-- EXPECT: STANDING make an order on the application
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(a) the court may make an order dismissing the application` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(1)(a) the court may make an order dismissing the application` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 20(2) -- the reach and the terms of an order`

-- Positional construction of an order the court has made: its kind; the day it was made; whom it reaches; the last day of any time limit.
`an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit` MEANS `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity`, (YMD 2026 3 1), `a particular registered charity`, NOTHING
`an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026` MEANS `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity`, (YMD 2026 3 1), `a particular registered charity`, JUST (YMD 2026 12 31)
`an order of the court dismissing the application, made on 1 March 2026` MEANS `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order dismissing the application`, (YMD 2026 3 1), `a particular registered charity`, NOTHING
`an order of the court for a description of charities` MEANS `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor`, (YMD 2026 3 1), `a description of registered charities`, NOTHING
`an order of the court for all registered charities` MEANS `Order made by the court under Article 20(1)` OF `an order requiring a registered charity to suspend or remove the governor`, (YMD 2026 3 1), `all registered charities`, NOTHING

-- src:521 | (2) An order under paragraph (1) may, without limitation –
-- src:522 | (a) apply to a governor in respect of a particular registered charity, a description of registered charities or all registered charities;
-- (2)(a) An order may apply to a governor in respect of a particular registered charity, a description of registered charities or all registered charities.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(a) the order applies to the charity` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(2)(a) the order applies to the charity` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(a) the order applies to the charity` `an order of the court for a description of charities` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(2)(a) the order applies to the charity` `an order of the court for a description of charities` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(a) the order applies to the charity` `an order of the court for all registered charities` FALSE FALSE

-- src:523 | (b) be made subject to any condition or time limit that appears to the court to be necessary or equitable.
-- (2)(b) An order may be made subject to any condition or time limit. The last day named in a time limit is inside the order on the reading taken (F6.22), outside it on the other.
-- Made on 1 March 2026: not in force the day before, in force from that day.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `the readings taken` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit` (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `the readings taken` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit` (YMD 2026 3 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `the readings taken` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit` (YMD 2090 1 1)
-- With a time limit ending on 31 December 2026.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `the readings taken` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026` (YMD 2026 12 30)
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `the readings taken` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` `the readings taken` `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026` (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026` (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT       `Art 20(2)(b) the order of the court is in force on the day` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026` (YMD 2026 12 30)

-- src:517 | (c) an order that the entity must not be registered as a charity;
-- IP24: the court has ordered that the entity must not be registered: an order of kind (c) that is in force on the day.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` (LIST `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit`) (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` (LIST `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit`) (YMD 2026 2 28)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` (LIST `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026`) (YMD 2027 1 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` (LIST `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026`) (YMD 2026 12 31)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` (`the readings taken but with F6.22 read as` `the permission ends before the day named`) (LIST `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with a time limit ending on 31 December 2026`) (YMD 2026 12 31)
-- An order of another kind is not the order that the entity must not be registered; no orders, no such order.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` (LIST `an order of the court dismissing the application, made on 1 March 2026`) (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` EMPTY (YMD 2026 6 1)
#ASSERT       `Art 20(1)(c) the court orders that the entity must not be registered` `the readings taken` (LIST `an order of the court dismissing the application, made on 1 March 2026`, `an order of the court that the entity must not be registered, made on 1 March 2026, with no time limit`) (YMD 2026 6 1)

§§ `Article 20(3) -- who may apply for a disqualification order`

-- src:524 | (3) If it appears to the Commissioner or the Attorney General that it is or may be expedient in the public interest that a person should not, without the leave of the court, be a governor of or in any way whether directly or indirectly be concerned or take part in the management of a registered charity, the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply to the court for an order to that effect against the person (a “disqualification order”).
-- (3) If it appears to the Commissioner or the Attorney General that it is or may be expedient in the public interest ..., the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply to the court for an order.
-- Reading taken (F6.23): each may apply on its own view. Both of the same view: both may apply.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court for a disqualification order` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `apply to the court for a disqualification order` `the Attorney General` AT 9
-- It appears to the Commissioner only: the Commissioner may apply; on the reading taken the Attorney General may not (the Attorney General is not of the view).
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court for a disqualification order
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- It appears to the Attorney General only: the discriminating case of F6.23. The Commissioner may not on the reading taken ...
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- ... but may on the other reading, where the view of either lets either apply.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner may apply for a disqualification order` (`the readings taken but with F6.23 read as` `the view of either the Commissioner or the Attorney General`) FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court for a disqualification order` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court for a disqualification order
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner may apply for a disqualification order` (`the readings taken but with F6.23 read as` `the view of either the Commissioner or the Attorney General`) FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING apply to the court for a disqualification order
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` (`the readings taken but with F6.23 read as` `the view of either the Commissioner or the Attorney General`) TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Neither of that view: neither may apply, on either reading.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner may apply for a disqualification order` (`the readings taken but with F6.23 read as` `the view of either the Commissioner or the Attorney General`) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` (`the readings taken but with F6.23 read as` `the view of either the Commissioner or the Attorney General`) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

-- The same power through the one rule that names the applicant. Any other applicant has no power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` `the Commissioner` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `apply to the court for a disqualification order` `the Commissioner` AT 9
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` `the Attorney General` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Attorney General` DOES `apply to the court for a disqualification order` `the Attorney General` AT 9
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(3) the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply for a disqualification order` `the readings taken` `a governor` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 20(4) -- when the court may make a disqualification order`

-- src:526 | (a) the person’s conduct in relation to a registered charity, or to an entity applying for registration; or
-- src:527 | (b) the seriousness of a reportable matter in relation to the person.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(4)(a) the person is unfit by virtue of the person's conduct` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(4)(a) the person is unfit by virtue of the person's conduct` FALSE
#ASSERT       `Art 20(4)(b) the person is unfit by virtue of the seriousness of a reportable matter` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(4)(b) the person is unfit by virtue of the seriousness of a reportable matter` FALSE
-- src:525 | (4) The court may, on such an application or on an application under Article 19(9)(b) or (13), make a disqualification order if it is satisfied that the person is unfit to be concerned in the management of a registered charity, by virtue of –
-- (4) The court may, on such an application or on an application under Article 19(9)(b) or (13), make a disqualification order if it is satisfied that the person is unfit ... by virtue of (a) or (b).
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make a disqualification order` `the court` AT 9
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the court` DOES `make a disqualification order` `the court` AT 9
-- EXPECT: STANDING make a disqualification order
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Each ground alone leaves the power standing (not only both together).
-- EXPECT: STANDING make a disqualification order
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: STANDING make a disqualification order
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- Satisfied of neither ground, or no application: the court has no such power.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` TRUE FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(4) the court may make a disqualification order` FALSE TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)

§§ `Article 20(5) -- the period of a disqualification order`

-- src:528 | (5) A disqualification order is to be for such period, not exceeding 15 years, as the court directs.
-- (5) A disqualification order is to be for such period, not exceeding 15 years, as the court directs.
-- The latest last day for an order beginning on 1 March 2026: the anniversary, 1 March 2041, on the reading taken; the day before on the third reading.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` `the readings taken` (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2041 3 1
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2041 2 28
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) (YMD 2026 3 1) EQUALS YMD 2041 3 1
-- An order beginning on 29 February 2028 (the discriminating case of F6.14): 28 February 2043 on the reading taken, 1 March 2043 where 29 February rolls, 27 February 2043 where the day before the anniversary is the last day.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` `the readings taken` (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2043 2 28
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2043 3 1
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the latest last day of a disqualification order beginning on` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) (YMD 2028 2 29) EQUALS YMD 2043 2 27

-- Positional construction of an order: the person; the first day; the last day.
`an order of 15 years against Zed` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2041 3 1
`an order of 16 years against Zed` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2042 3 1
`an order against Zed one day over 15 years` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2041 3 2
`an order of 5 years against Zed` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2026 3 1, YMD 2031 3 1
`an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 1 March 2043` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2028 2 29, YMD 2043 3 1
`an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 28 February 2043` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2028 2 29, YMD 2043 2 28

#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order of 15 years against Zed`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order of 16 years against Zed`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order against Zed one day over 15 years`
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order of 5 years against Zed`
-- Fifteen years exactly is within the limit on the first two readings and over it on the third, which counts the first day as day one.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `an order of 15 years against Zed`
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `an order of 5 years against Zed`
-- The leap-day order: valid under the rolling reading only when it ends on 1 March; ending on 28 February it is valid under the first two and not under the third.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 1 March 2043`
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) `an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 1 March 2043`
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` `the readings taken` `an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 28 February 2043`
#ASSERT       `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the anniversary, and 29 February rolls to 1 March`) `an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 28 February 2043`
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(5) the order's period is within the limit` (`the readings taken but with F6.14 read as` `the last day is the day before the anniversary`) `an order against Zed from 29 February 2028 to 28 February 2043`

§§ `Article 20(6) -- contravening a disqualification order`

-- (6) A person who contravenes a disqualification order commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for 2 years and to a fine.
-- Zed is bound from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030, first and last days included. Contravening: acting as a governor (or in the management) within those days, without leave.
`an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` MEANS `Disqualification order` OF "Zed", YMD 2025 1 1, YMD 2030 12 31
-- src:524 | (3) If it appears to the Commissioner or the Attorney General that it is or may be expedient in the public interest that a person should not, without the leave of the court, be a governor of or in any way whether directly or indirectly be concerned or take part in the management of a registered charity, the Commissioner or the Attorney General may apply to the court for an order to that effect against the person (a “disqualification order”).
-- src:529 | (6) A person who contravenes a disqualification order commits an offence and is liable to imprisonment for 2 years and to a fine.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2025 1 1) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2030 12 31) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2024 12 31) TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2031 1 1) TRUE FALSE
-- With the leave of the court, or when the person is not a governor or concerned in management, or another person: no contravention.
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Zed" (YMD 2026 6 1) FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) the person contravenes the disqualification order` `an order against Zed from 1 January 2025 to 31 December 2030` "Yan" (YMD 2026 6 1) TRUE FALSE
-- The offence is the contravention (the paragraph states no excuse).
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) the person commits an offence` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) the person commits an offence` FALSE
-- The prohibition: being a governor or concerned in management while the order binds is the failure.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 20(6)
#TRACE `Art 20(6) a person must not contravene a disqualification order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `be a governor of, or be concerned or take part in the management of, a registered charity` `any person` AT 4
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 20(6) a person must not contravene a disqualification order` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `be a governor of, or be concerned or take part in the management of, a registered charity` `any person` AT 4
-- EXPECT: STANDING be a governor of, or be concerned or take part in the management of, a registered charity
#TRACE `Art 20(6) a person must not contravene a disqualification order` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 20(6)
#TRACE `Art 20(6) the standing prohibition of a disqualification order` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `any person` DOES `be a governor of, or be concerned or take part in the management of, a registered charity` `any person` AT 4
-- The penalty is data: up to 24 months (2 years) and a fine for which the Law states no maximum.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) the penalty for contravening a disqualification order` EQUALS `Penalty provided` OF (JUST 24), `a fine with no maximum stated in the Law`
-- F6.16, the unit of "2 years": from 1 March 2027 twenty-four calendar months end on 1 March 2029, 731 days later (2028 is a leap year); 730 days is within on both; 731 only on the calendar-months reading.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 731
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` (`the readings taken but with F6.16 read as` `days`) (YMD 2027 3 1) 731
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 730
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` (`the readings taken but with F6.16 read as` `days`) (YMD 2027 3 1) 730
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` `the readings taken` (YMD 2027 3 1) 732
-- From 1 March 2025 twenty-four calendar months end on 1 March 2027, 730 days later: 730 days is within, 731 is not, on both readings.
#ASSERT       `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` `the readings taken` (YMD 2025 3 1) 730
#ASSERT NOT   `Art 20(6) a term of days from the start is within the maximum of two years` `the readings taken` (YMD 2025 3 1) 731
